  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dukire Twubake-To heal to build: Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Dukire Twubake Phase II project supports reconciliation and inclusion in Burundi by strengthening trauma healing, social cohesion, and community resilience. It provides psychosocial support, intergenerational dialogues, and explicitly tailored assistance to women, youth, persons with disabilities, ex combatants, and other marginalised groups. The project also builds leadership, advocacy, and livelihood skills, enabling communities to pursue social, economic, and political opportunities. Finally, it connects communities with local and national decision makers through exchanges, field visits, and a national forum to help integrate trauma informed and inclusive governance practices into policy processes.</narrative>
  </description>
